    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0848" n="1682" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/904</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-29T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4270. For McFadden [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 104. Your No. 103, Embassy 3942, May 21, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d732-f1"
                    /> We approve in principle the plan for creation of inter-Allied committee at
                    Madrid to consider proposed imports from Associated nations and to cooperate
                    closely with Inter-Allied Bureau of Purchases, Madrid, so that status of
                    applications to export from Spain may be considered in connection with Spanish
                    requests for imports into Spain from Associated nations. We note that the plan
                    as set out in your cable does not appear to contemplate Italian representative.
                    We feel that for political reasons Italy should be given an opportunity to name
                    a representative on any inter-Allied committee set up in Spain. We are cabling
                        Sheldon and
                        Chadbourne our views
                    as above set out and are authorizing Sheldon, if he can
                    appropriately do so, to discuss the matter with the British with a view to
                    obtaining their adherence to the plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d732-f1" n="1" xml:id="d732-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for a fuller explanation of the plan in question, see telegram from
                    the Chargé in Great Britain, No. 10390, June 3, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
